Alongside <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a>, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS Golden Gate</a>, Apple today released new software for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod-mini/">HomePod mini</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/11/homepods-red.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-922235" /><br/>
&zwnj;HomePod&zwnj; Software 27 adds <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/airplay/">AirPlay</a> improvements and support for AutoMix when listening to <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a>.<br/>
<blockquote>This update introduces support for AutoMix with Apple Music, which transitions between songs like a DJ does, time stretching and beatmatching to deliver a continuous playback experience. It also delivers improved AirPlay performance, providing faster and more responsive connections when sharing music from iPhone, iPad, or Mac, and provides bug fixes and security updates for your HomePod.</blockquote><br/>
